# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# A loft from a circle to a square through a rail tied to Intersect points,
# and a loose rail's miss in words (mitcad#1944; docs/ui-conventions.md
# "What a message says"), on loft-rail-intersect.json (Sketch1 F1: a 20 mm
# circle; Sketch2 F3 40 mm up: a 20 mm square; Sketch3 F4 on XZ: the rail
# c4 between the circle's and the square's Intersect points p1 and p3,
# meeting the square in its side's middle, and the loose rail c5 ending
# 0.3 mm outside the square):
#   1. Loft through the circle and the square with the rail c4: the
#      sections' edges do not line up at the rail, the loft is matched from
#      it and builds (Loft1).
#   2. A loft through the loose rail (Loft2, sent as a model command) fails;
#      edited from the timeline, the panel says how far the rail misses the
#      square in words, no names or coordinates, and the pointer over the
#      message paints its two places (the nearest points on the rail and
#      the square).
#   3. Esc cancels the edit.
# Run by tools/ui-loft-rail-intersect-test.sh (Linux),
# tools/ui-windows-loft-rail-intersect-test.ps1 (Windows) and
# tools/ui-macos-loft-rail-intersect-test.sh (macOS).
expect-ever 'View area'
wait-idle
# Seen from the side and above: the square 40 mm up does not hide the
# circle (as it does from the top), and the rail's sketch plane is not
# edge on.
command view.iso
wait-idle
command view.fit
wait-idle

# 1. The loft through the rail tied to the Intersect points.
mark
command solid.loft
wait-log '^Command Loft started'
wait-idle
click-pick 'profile F1/'
wait-log '^Loft Profiles: 1 profile'
wait-idle
click-pick 'profile F3/'
wait-log '^Loft Profiles: 2 profiles'
wait-idle
mark
qt-choice input_guide 'Rails'
wait-log '^Panel Loft input rails[.]0[.]path at ' 10
wait-idle
click-logged '^Panel Loft input rails[.]0[.]path at '
wait-idle
expect-ever '^Sketch entity F4/c4 at '
click-logged '^Sketch entity F4/c4 at '
wait-log '^Loft Rail: 1 sketch curve [[]sketch curve c4 of F4[]]' 10
wait-log '^Preview Loft: ok' 60
wait-idle
expect-no-log '^Panel Loft error: '
mark
key Return
wait-log '^Added loft [(]New Body[)] through 2 sections' 60
wait-idle

# 2. The loose rail: refused in words, its places on hover.
mark
model-command '{"cmd":"add_feature","def":{"type":"loft","sections":[{"type":"profile","sketch":"F1","region":"r{c1}"},{"type":"profile","sketch":"F3","region":"r{c1[c4,c2],c2[c1,c3],c3[c2,c4],c4[c3,c1]}"}],"rails":[{"sketch":"F4","curves":["c5"]}],"operation":"new_body"}}'
wait-log '^Timeline Loft2 at ' 30
wait-idle
mark
dblclick-logged '^Timeline Loft2 at '
wait-log '^Editing F[0-9]+ with Loft$'
wait-log '^Panel Loft error: .*rail 1 misses the second profile by 0[.]3 mm$' 60
wait-log '^Panel Loft message at ' 10
wait-idle
expect-never '^Panel Loft (error|message box): .*([EV][{]|r[{]|F[0-9]|section [0-9]|[(]-?[0-9.]+, )'
mark
hover-logged '^Panel Loft message at '
wait-log '^Panel Loft message hovered: 2 places$' 10
mark
leave-widget commandMessage
wait-log '^Notice hover highlighted: none$' 10
wait-idle

# 3. Esc cancels.
mark
key Escape
wait-log '^Command Loft cancelled$'
wait-idle
